==================================================
25. KEY POINTS TO REMEMBER
==================================================

1. Decision Tree Regression is a supervised learning
   algorithm for predicting a continuous target.

2. It uses decision rules to split the dataset.

3. The first split starts at the ROOT node.

4. Internal nodes contain decisions.

5. Branches represent outcomes of decisions.

6. Leaf nodes produce predictions.

7. A common regression prediction at a leaf is the mean
   target value of the samples in that leaf.

8. A common splitting criterion is reduction in MSE.

9. Decision Trees can model nonlinear relationships.

10. Feature scaling is generally NOT required.

11. max_depth controls tree depth.

12. min_samples_split controls when a node can be split.

13. min_samples_leaf controls the minimum samples in a leaf.

14. Very deep trees can overfit.

15. Very shallow trees can underfit.

16. Decision Tree Regression produces piecewise constant
    predictions.

17. Random Forest Regression builds on the idea of
    combining many decision trees.